--
--
N5008 [temp.constr.decl]/3 -- the associated constraints of a
constrained member of a class template include the enclosing class
template's parameters; a requires atom referencing them
(__is_constructible(T2, U2) inside pr<T2>) is now evaluated by mapping
the class instance's ID_C_template/ID_C_template_arguments in the
satisfaction check, so the unviable constrained constructor is removed
and pr(const T2&) converts the literal 0 as a null pointer constant.
g++/clang++ runtime-verified.
